{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEMxHZuJYMvap3dvknNF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found one real authorization hole and fixed it. A user could \"like\" or \"view\" someone else's private task.\n\n- **The hole:** `POST /tasks/{id}/like` and `/view` skipped the visibility check. Bob could bump the like and view counts on Alice's private task #1 and get a 200. Every other endpoint already returned 403 for him. I added the same `can_access` check that `comments` and `nudge` use (`api.py`).\n- **A smaller issue:** `PATCH /tasks/{id}` accepted any value for `visibility` or `title`. It now returns 400 for a bad visibility or an empty or non-string title. That one only affects the task's owner, not other users.\n- **Checks that held up:** missing or unknown tokens get 401, malformed JSON gets 400, and unknown routes or tasks get 404. Read, edit, delete, comment, complete and nudge on a private task all return 403 for a non-owner. Users can't set `owner` or the counters through create or PATCH.\n- **Tests:** I added two tests in `tests/test_api.py`. One has Bob try every action on Alice's private task and checks that nothing changed. The other covers the PATCH validation. All 7 tests pass. With the old `api.py`, 2 of the 7 fail.\n- **Not run live:** I didn't probe the server on port 60320. The tests use an in-process copy of the same handler.\n- **Before launch:** the README's dev tokens are static, so replace them. There's also no rate limiting on likes and views of public tasks.\n\nANSWER.md has the full write-up, including which parts of your colleague's note applied. I used their cross-user matrix idea. I skipped installing paranoid-qa, the injection pass and the premium-flag check, because installs weren't allowed and this API has no database or such fields."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1086,"cache_read_input_tokens":27890,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1086},"output_tokens":592,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e1921eac-7adf-407e-ba92-0619001d9c83","uuid":"c9c7783c-1182-4c47-84ce-60cfe61cbb5a","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:32:27.922Z","request_id":"req_011CgEMxHHJHEQLPLmGgDugD"}
